# QUESTION : GRACEFUL DEGRADATION KYA HAI ?
=============================================

Graceful Degradation ek aisa approach hai jisme jab system ka koi non-critical component fail ho jaata hai,
to poora application fail hone ke bajaye limited functionality ke saath kaam karta rehta hai
yaani ek feature sacrifice karte hain, poora system nahi.

Graceful Degradation kaam karne ke liye pehle ye clear karna padta hai ki
kaunsa component critical hai aur kaunsa non-critical.

Socho ek e-commerce application hai. Uske andar multiple services hain:

- Product Service (critical — product dikhana zaroori hai)
- Order Service (critical — order lena zaroori hai)
- Recommendation Service (non-critical — "aapko ye bhi pasand aa sakta hai")
- Review Service (non-critical — reviews dikhana)
- Rewards Service (non-critical — points credit karna)

Ab maan lo Recommendation Service crash ho gayi, ,toh user ko ye nahi bolna chahiye:

❌ "Website unavailable"

Instead:

✅ Products dikhao
✅ User ko purchase karne do
❌ Recommendations mat dikhao

Yaani non-critical feature ko sacrifice karke core functionality ko alive rakha.


## QUESTION : KAISE IMPLEMENT KARTE HAI ?
------------------------------------------

1: FEATURE FLAG
-----------------
- Feature flags ek on/off switch ki tarah hote hain. Agar koi non-critical feature problem kar raha hai, 
  toh hum us feature ko OFF kar sakte hain. Ye flag application configuration (application.properties etc.), 
  DB, ya dedicated feature-flag system mein maintain ho sakta hai. Isse non-critical feature disable ho jaata hai, 
  lekin baaki core functionality normally chalti rehti hai.

- Example: Maan lo Recommendation Service mein problem aa gayi -> Feature flag OFF → recommendation feature disable -> Product browsing/order/payment normally chalte rahenge.


2: TIMEOUT
------------

- Agar non-critical service response dene mein bahut time le rahi hai, toh hum connection aur read timeout 
  configure kar sakte hain. Defined time ke andar response nahi aaya toh wait karna stop kar dete hain aur
  appropriate fallback response de dete hain. Isse slow dependency ki wajah se poori user request unnecessarily block nahi hoti.

- Example: Recommendation Service timeout → "Recommendations temporarily unavailable" → Products/order/payment functionality normally continue.


3: CIRCUIT BREAKER
--------------------

- Agar non-critical service fail ho jaati hai, toh Circuit Breaker us service ko temporarily call karna band 
  kar deta hai aur fallback response deta hai, jisse core system normally available rehta hai.


4: ASYNC OFFLOADING 
---------------------
- Agar koi non-critical service temporarily unavailable hai, toh request ko synchronously process karne ke bajaye
  queue mein daal sakte hain aur service available hone par baad mein process kar sakte hain.



## QUESTION : FALLBACK KYA HAI ?
---------------------------------
- Fallback ka matlab hai — agar koi non-critical operation complete nahi ho paata, toh us operation ke response 
  ki jagah ek default/preconfigured ya cached response diya jaata hai.

- Agar operation critical hai, toh generally explicit error return karte hain, kyunki stale ya incorrect fallback 
  data user ko galat decision lene par majboor kar sakta hai.

- Example:
  Recommendation Service fail -> Recommendation unavailable → Show popular products / previously cached recommendations to the user.

  Payment / Balance Service fail -> Payment / Balance unavailable → Proper Error Response




