# QUESTION : BULKHEAD PATTERN KYA HAI ?
==========================================

Bulkhead Pattern ek aisa approach hai jisme service ke available thread pool ko alag-alag pools mein isolate kiya jaata hai,
alag-alag downstream operations ke liye — taaki ek failing ya slow dependency calling service ke saare threads consume na kar sake.


## QUESTION : BULKHEAD PATTERN KE BINA PROBLEM HOTI HAI ?
------------------------------------------------------------
- Suppose Order Service ke paas Tomcat thread pool me total 200 threads hain (default).
- Ab maan lo Order Service Notification Service aur Payment Service dono ko internally call karti hai.
- Order Service har request ke liye thread pool se ek-ek thread allocate karti hai — Payment call ke liye alag thread, Notification call ke liye alag thread. 
- Maan lo Notification Service slow ho gayi.
- Kyunki Payment Service up and running hai, Payment operation complete hone ke baad thread release ho jaata hai aur thread pool me wapas return ho jaata hai — matlab woh thread dobara use ho sakta hai. 
- Lekin kyunki Notification Service slow hai, Notification call karne wali thread Notification Service ka response aane tak wait karti rehti hai — release nahi hoti.
- Jaise-jaise Notification bhejne wali nayi requests aati hain, unke liye bhi thread pool se naye threads allocate hote rehte hain, aur ye threads bhi Notification Service ke response ka wait karte hue block ho jaate hain.
- Dheere-dheere poora thread pool exhaust ho jaata hai. 
- Ab aane wali Payment process karne wali requests ke liye koi thread bacha hi nahi — kyunki saare threads Notification Service ke wait me blocked hain. 
- Isliye Payment operation bhi fail hone lagta hai. 
- Yaani Notification Service ke slow hone ki wajah se Payment operation bhi affected ho jaata hai — yehi Cascading Effect hai.


### SOLUTION — BULKHEAD PATTERN 
---------------------------------

Bulkhead Pattern me service ke available thread pool ko alag-alag pools me isolate kiya jaata hai — alag-alag downstream operations ke liye.

Client → Order Service (200 Tomcat threads)
              ↓
    ┌─────────┼─────────┐
    ↓         ↓         ↓
 Pool A    Pool B    Pool C
 (50)      (30)      (20)
    ↓         ↓         ↓
 Payment  Notification  Fraud


- Pool A (50 threads) → sirf Payment Service calls ke liye
- Pool B (30 threads) → sirf Notification Service calls ke liye
- Pool C (20 threads) → sirf Fraud Service calls ke liye


Ab agar Notification Service slow ho gayi, to sirf Pool B ke 30 threads block honge. 
Pool A aur Pool C khali rahenge, isliye Payment aur Fraud calls normally chalti rahengi,
aur Order Service zinda rehti hai. Bas ek dependency ka failure isolate ho jaata hai — doosri dependencies effect nahi hoti hai.
